From: X710 bring-up <bringup@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] i2c: qcom-geni: re-arm the serial engine on samsung,reset-before-trans

Samsung's SM-X710 device tree marks the QUP2 SE7 I2C controller that hosts the
EF-DX710 pogo keyboard with samsung,reset-before-trans (and stop-after-trans),
and its downstream geni driver reloads the serial engine before every transfer
because of it.

Without that, mainline binds the keyboard, drives its rail and pulses its reset,
and the STM32 still never answers: every read returns -ENXIO (a clean NACK, so
the bus is idle rather than stuck) and a quick-write scan of the whole adapter
finds no device at any address, while TWRP's stock kernel on the same tablet, the
same controller and the same two pins enumerates the cover as
EF-DX710_v1.4.1.0, con:1/1, model_id 0x2 in the same session (test 045).

The data sheet level reason is not documented; the behaviour is.  Reloading the
SE firmware is the closest mainline equivalent of the vendor's controller reset -
it is exactly what probe does once - and geni_load_se_firmware() is already
exported, so this stays inside the I2C driver and is gated by the DT property, so
no other board is affected.  qcom_geni_i2c_conf() re-applies the I2C packing and
watermarks directly after.
---
diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
index d2f5055b0..f77e24c45 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-qcom-geni.c
@@ -119,6 +119,7 @@ struct geni_i2c_dev {
 	bool gpi_mode;
 	bool abort_done;
 	bool is_tx_multi_desc_xfer;
+	bool reset_before_trans;
 	u32 num_msgs;
 	struct geni_i2c_gpi_multi_desc_xfer i2c_multi_desc_config;
 };
@@ -921,6 +922,22 @@ static int geni_i2c_xfer(struct i2c_adapter *adap,
 		return ret;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Boards that ask for samsung,reset-before-trans want the serial engine
+	 * reloaded before each transfer, exactly as probe leaves it.  Reloading
+	 * the SE firmware resets the controller and its RAM configuration;
+	 * qcom_geni_i2c_conf() below re-applies the I2C packing and watermarks.
+	 */
+	if (gi2c->reset_before_trans) {
+		ret = geni_load_se_firmware(&gi2c->se, GENI_SE_I2C);
+		if (ret) {
+			dev_err(gi2c->se.dev, "error re-arming the SE: %d\n", ret);
+			pm_runtime_put_noidle(gi2c->se.dev);
+			pm_runtime_set_suspended(gi2c->se.dev);
+			return ret;
+		}
+	}
+
 	qcom_geni_i2c_conf(gi2c);
 
 	if (gi2c->gpi_mode)
@@ -1055,6 +1072,13 @@ static int geni_i2c_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	gi2c->adap.dev.parent = dev;
 	gi2c->adap.dev.of_node = dev->of_node;
 	strscpy(gi2c->adap.name, "Geni-I2C", sizeof(gi2c->adap.name));
+	/*
+	 * Some boards need the serial engine re-armed before every transfer.
+	 * Samsung's SM-X710 node asks for it with samsung,reset-before-trans,
+	 * and without it the pogo keyboard's STM32 never answers.
+	 */
+	gi2c->reset_before_trans =
+		of_property_read_bool(dev->of_node, "samsung,reset-before-trans");
 
 	ret = geni_icc_get(&gi2c->se, desc ? desc->icc_ddr : "qup-memory");
 	if (ret)
